{″}(0),$ ${f}^{‴}(0)$ and ${f}^{(4)}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{1-3x}=(1-3x)^{-1} & ⟹ &  & f(0) & =1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =3(1-3x)^{-2} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =3 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =18(1-3x)^{-3} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =18 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =162(1-3x)^{-4} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =162 \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(x) & =1944(1-3x)^{-5} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{(4)}(0) & =1944\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${P}_{4}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{4}(x) & =1+(3)\\cdot x+\\frac{18}{2!}{x}^{2}+\\frac{162}{3!}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1944}{4!}{x}^{4} \\\\  & =1+3x+9{x}^{2}+27{x}^{3}+81{x}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535194 true] [17592186336824 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336825 13194139535194 true] [17592186336824 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535194 true] [17592186336824 1041 "field-1" 13194139535194 true] [17592186336824 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336825 13194139535194 true] [17592186336824 1110 #uuid "617492cf-d542-5add-8a4a-82f6333583bb" 13194139535194 true] [17592186336825 1034 "9x^2+27x^3" 13194139535194 true] [17592186336825 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535194 true] [17592186336825 1111 #uuid "3388e9c3-36ca-5021-a9a8-0c9ba1daca3d" 13194139535194 true] [17592186336826 1017 #edb/ref 17592186336827 13194139535194 true] [17592186336826 1017 #edb/ref 17592186336830 13194139535194 true] [17592186336826 1089 "q-351793" 13194139535194 true] [17592186336826 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535194 true] [17592186336826 1100 "Find the fourth-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{4}(x)$ of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ about $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\n${P}_{4}(x)=-1\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n${(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n${(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{4}$" 13194139535194 true] [17592186336826 1113 #uuid "5441dd9f-8972-5d8d-be50-ca0a48e5feaf" 13194139535194 true] [17592186336826 1145 "The fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{4}(x)= & \\,f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(a)}{3!}(x-a)^{3} \\\\  & \\,+\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(a)}{4!}(x-a)^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $a=\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{4}(x)= & \\,f(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\frac{{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}{2!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{2} \\\\  & \\,+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}{3!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{3}+\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}{4!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need to work out $f(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),$ ${f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),$ ${f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),$ ${f}^{‴}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ and ${f}^{(4)}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & ⟹ &  & f\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )=0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=9 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =27\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =27\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )=0 \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(x) & =81\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{(4)}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =81\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${P}_{4}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{4}(x) & =-1+0(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\frac{9}{2!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{2}+0{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{3}-\\frac{81}{4!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{4} \\\\  & =-1+\\frac{9}{2}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{2}-\\frac{27}{8}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535194 true] [17592186336827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336828 13194139535194 true] [17592186336827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186336829 13194139535194 true] [17592186336827 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535194 true] [17592186336827 1041 "field-1" 13194139535194 true] [17592186336827 1104 #edb/ref 17592186336828 13194139535194 true] [17592186336827 1110 #uuid "ef5ec9d3-6bca-56fe-9c6d-60a56c6bda56" 13194139535194 true] [175921